<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<!-- Partial Info.plist, MERGED with the generated one.

	     GENERATE_INFOPLIST_FILE stays YES: every usage-description string and
	     the scene manifest still live in build settings, exactly as before.
	     This file exists for one key that build settings cannot express.

	     Xcode's plist generator only writes an allowlist of INFOPLIST_KEY_*
	     settings, and array-valued keys are not on it. Setting
	     INFOPLIST_KEY_UIBackgroundModes = audio is silently accepted, appears
	     in -showBuildSettings, and never reaches the built plist — verified
	     2026-08-24 with `plutil -extract` on the built app.

	     Why the app needs it: the rest alarm plays real audio so the sound
	     reaches AirPods (a UNNotificationSound does not). The moment that
	     matters most is the screen being off mid-workout, and starting
	     playback from the background requires this mode. Without it
	     AVAudioSession activation fails there and the alarm is silent again —
	     the exact bug it was added to fix. -->
	<key>UIBackgroundModes</key>
	<array>
		<string>audio</string>
	</array>
</dict>
</plist>
